{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mq6rpqlc","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/cloude","title":"orch-gate.sh false-positives background subagents' inline edits (session_id mismatch)","summary":"FINDING (2026-06-08, surfaced by the bench-report subagent): the PreToolUse gate hooks/orch-gate.sh blocks Write/Edit for a DISPATCHED BACKGROUND SUBAGENT even after it legitimately start_task-claimed the task. Cause: the gate authorizes by querying /active-claim?session=<harness session_id of the calling conversation>, but a background worker's claim is recorded under its agent_id/task, not that harness session_id — so the gate sees no claim and blocks. The documented escape hatch ORCH_GATE_OFF=1 can't be injected from the subagent's Bash env into the hook process. Workaround used: write to /tmp then `cp` (Bash isn't gated). Impact: directly contradicts the workspace norm ('dispatch substantive work to background subagents that edit inline') — every such subagent hits this. Fix candidates: gate should accept a claim keyed by the worker's agent_id/task (not just harness session_id); or recognize background-worker context; or provide a per-task claim token the worker passes. Note: in the desktop app no settings.json hooks run for the MAIN agent, but subagents are still being gated.","created_by":"main","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-10T19:01:05.747Z"}
{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mq6rpqlc","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/cloude","title":"orch-gate.sh false-positives background subagents' inline edits (session_id mismatch)","summary":"FINDING (2026-06-08, surfaced by the bench-report subagent): the PreToolUse gate hooks/orch-gate.sh blocks Write/Edit for a DISPATCHED BACKGROUND SUBAGENT even after it legitimately start_task-claimed the task. Cause: the gate authorizes by querying /active-claim?session=<harness session_id of the calling conversation>, but a background worker's claim is recorded under its agent_id/task, not that harness session_id — so the gate sees no claim and blocks. The documented escape hatch ORCH_GATE_OFF=1 can't be injected from the subagent's Bash env into the hook process. Workaround used: write to /tmp then `cp` (Bash isn't gated). Impact: directly contradicts the workspace norm ('dispatch substantive work to background subagents that edit inline') — every such subagent hits this. Fix candidates: gate should accept a claim keyed by the worker's agent_id/task (not just harness session_id); or recognize background-worker context; or provide a per-task claim token the worker passes. Note: in the desktop app no settings.json hooks run for the MAIN agent, but subagents are still being gated.","created_by":"main","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-10T19:08:57.822Z"}
